# What Vercel must not upload.
#
# Learned the hard way, 20 August 2026: the Vercel CLI does NOT read
# .gitignore. It reads this file. Without it, `vercel deploy` tried to
# upload the 6.2 GB Turborepo cache before starting the build, produced no
# output for ten minutes, and never registered a deployment at all. The
# actual source this project needs is 764 files and 7.3 MB.
#
# Everything below is either regenerated by Vercel's own build or must
# never leave this machine. Nothing here is needed to build the app:
# Vercel installs dependencies and builds from source itself.
#
# Patterns follow .gitignore syntax, so a bare name matches at any depth.

# Build caches and outputs. Vercel rebuilds all of these.
node_modules
.turbo
.next
dist
.vercel

# Secrets. These hold the Supabase service role key and the engine's
# gateway key. They belong in Vercel's environment variable settings and
# nowhere else, least of all inside a deployment bundle.
.env.local
.env.engine.local
.env.development.local
.env.production.local
.env.test.local

# Local noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
